        "candidate_id": "C_10d0b3ac8696b303_0",
        "edit": "Removed the duplicate 3'd6 case item (which caused a case-item collision) and removed the stray empty statements in the always block; the default branch now handles all other inputs, so ABC=0 produces X=0,Y=1 as expected.",
        "lens_id": "generic_v1",
        "replacement_rtl": "module JG3(ABC,X,Y);\n\t\n\tinput [2:0] ABC;\n\t\n\toutput X, Y;\n\treg X, Y;\n\t\n\talways@(ABC)\n\t\tcase(ABC)\n\t\t\t3'd0: begin X<=0;Y<=1; end\n\t\t\t3'd5: begin X<=1;Y=0; end\n\t\t\t3'd6: begin X<=1;Y=0; end\n\t\t\tdefault: begin X<=0;Y<=0; end\n\t\tendcase\t\n\t\nendmodule",
